WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.978 --> 00:00:17.180
One late autumn day, John hitched me to the high-wheeled cart.

2
00:00:19.121 --> 00:00:22.303
Then he and the squire climbed in and we drove out through the gate.

3
00:00:23.424 --> 00:00:25.965
The squire had to go to a certain town on business.

4
00:00:27.246 --> 00:00:30.168
The town was several hours away, but I didn't mind the work.

5
00:00:32.896 --> 00:00:36.377
The cart was light and easy to pull, and the weather was brisk and cool.

6
00:00:37.617 --> 00:00:40.798
It had rained a lot recently, so there were puddles everywhere.

7
00:00:41.899 --> 00:00:45.179
The wind blew fallen leaves across the road in colorful showers.

8
00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:50.201
Soon we reached the first toll bridge.

9
00:00:52.562 --> 00:00:54.462
The river was high because of all the rain.

10
00:00:55.462 --> 00:00:58.303
The flat wooden bridge was just a few inches above the water.

11
00:00:59.383 --> 00:01:01.064
The toll keeper stepped out of his hut.

12
00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:04.910
"The river's still rising," he told the squire and John.

13
00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:07.632
"I'm afraid it could be a bad night."

14
00:01:09.214 --> 00:01:10.595
The squire looked out at the bridge.

15
00:01:10.615 --> 00:01:15.018
"Your bridge has strong rails on both sides," he said.

16
00:01:15.038 --> 00:01:17.660
"I doubt you'll have any trouble here.

17
00:01:18.521 --> 00:01:19.342
But we'll be careful."

18
00:01:21.884 --> 00:01:23.985
We crossed the bridge and continued on our way.

19
00:01:26.307 --> 00:01:30.678
When we reached the town, John took me to a local stable to rest and eat while the

20
00:01:30.698 --> 00:01:32.419
squire went to take care of his business.

21
00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:36.581
By the time the squire reappeared, it was late afternoon.

22
00:01:37.722 --> 00:01:38.602
We started for home.

23
00:01:38.622 --> 00:01:44.086
"The wind is getting worse," John said as we drove out of town.

24
00:01:46.967 --> 00:01:50.890
"I don't think we've ever been out in such a terrible storm!"

25
00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:54.692
The road passed some fields and then entered a forest.

26
00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:01.222
The wind whipped the tree branches around overhead, making me a little nervous.

27
00:02:03.843 --> 00:02:05.904
The squire also sounded nervous as he spoke.

28
00:02:05.924 --> 00:02:09.845
"I wish we were out of this forest," he said.

29
00:02:09.865 --> 00:02:12.326
"Me too," John agreed.

30
00:02:13.447 --> 00:02:15.207
"I hope none of these branches fall on us."

31
00:02:16.328 --> 00:02:19.689
Just as he spoke, there was a loud crack above us.

32
00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:25.812
A second later a large limb crashed down onto the road ahead, blocking our way.

33
00:02:27.564 --> 00:02:29.805
The noise and surprise startled me terribly.

34
00:02:30.966 --> 00:02:32.247
I stopped short and trembled.

35
00:02:33.367 --> 00:02:35.568
Many horses would have spun around and run away.

36
00:02:36.529 --> 00:02:40.151
But I had learned not to do that, and so I stood as still as I could.

37
00:02:41.252 --> 00:02:43.093
John jumped out and hurried to my head.

38
00:02:43.113 --> 00:02:45.454
"Good boy," he said.

39
00:02:45.474 --> 00:02:47.355
"It's okay, there's nothing to fear.

40
00:02:48.436 --> 00:02:48.956
It missed us."

41
00:02:48.976 --> 00:02:53.158
"Yes, but barely," the squire said.

42
00:02:53.178 --> 00:02:55.399
"And now we can't go on.

43
00:02:55.659 --> 00:02:56.260
What should we do?"

44
00:02:58.272 --> 00:03:02.095
They decided we would have to go back to the last crossroads and take a different way home.

45
00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:07.119
We did just that, but it took a long time.

46
00:03:09.521 --> 00:03:12.684
By the time we reached the toll bridge again, it was almost dark.

47
00:03:13.725 --> 00:03:15.626
We approached the bridge at a steady walk.

48
00:03:16.607 --> 00:03:19.770
But as soon as my feet touched the wooden boards, I stopped short.

49
00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:23.132
I could feel that there was something different about the bridge.

50
00:03:23.973 --> 00:03:24.794
Something was wrong.

51
00:03:24.814 --> 00:03:28.504
"Go on, Beauty," called the squire.

52
00:03:29.565 --> 00:03:31.706
He flicked the whip lightly to urge me forward.

53
00:03:32.766 --> 00:03:35.567
But the bridge felt so strange, I stayed where I was.

54
00:03:36.708 --> 00:03:38.228
The squire flicked the whip again.

55
00:03:40.069 --> 00:03:43.111
It stung me a little harder this time, making me jump in place.

56
00:03:44.371 --> 00:03:47.292
Still I didn't dare take a step farther onto the bridge.

57
00:03:47.312 --> 00:03:50.234
"Wait, sir," John said.

58
00:03:50.254 --> 00:03:52.014
"Maybe there's something wrong."

59
00:03:53.615 --> 00:03:55.836
He jumped out of the cart and walked up to my head.

60
00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:57.981
"What's the matter, Beauty?"

61
00:03:58.281 --> 00:03:59.681
he asked in his soothing way.

62
00:03:59.701 --> 00:04:01.603
"Come on, let's go."

63
00:04:02.823 --> 00:04:06.285
At that moment the toll keeper burst out of his hut on the far side of the river.

64
00:04:07.366 --> 00:04:10.027
He waved a light around over his head and let out a shout.

65
00:04:11.388 --> 00:04:12.368
"Stop, stop!"

66
00:04:12.668 --> 00:04:13.169
he cried.

67
00:04:13.189 --> 00:04:15.010
"The bridge is broken in the middle.

68
00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:18.712
If you try to cross, you'll end up in the river!"

69
00:04:19.852 --> 00:04:20.853
"Oh my!"

70
00:04:21.193 --> 00:04:22.254
the squire exclaimed.

71
00:04:22.274 --> 00:04:23.614
"What a close call!"

72
00:04:23.634 --> 00:04:27.621
"Good boy," John murmured to me.

73
00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:30.383
He took me by the bridle and gently turned me around.

74
00:04:31.884 --> 00:04:35.807
Then he climbed back into the cart, and we continued down the river to the next bridge.

75
00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:41.472
It was built much higher over the water, and we crossed safely.

76
00:04:43.374 --> 00:04:46.276
When we finally arrived home, it was well after dark.

77
00:04:47.977 --> 00:04:50.700
We found the mistress waiting up for us despite the late hour.

78
00:04:52.781 --> 00:04:53.522
"Are you safe?"

79
00:04:54.002 --> 00:04:55.864
she cried, hurrying out to greet us.

80
00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:57.601
"I was so worried!"

81
00:04:57.621 --> 00:05:00.823
"Yes, my dear," the squire said.

82
00:05:00.843 --> 00:05:02.264
"We are safe.

83
00:05:02.765 --> 00:05:04.906
But only thanks to our fine Black Beauty.

84
00:05:06.327 --> 00:05:10.430
If he hadn't been wiser than John and me, we all would have been swept into the river

85
00:05:10.531 --> 00:05:11.131
and drowned."

86
00:05:12.632 --> 00:05:15.394
He went into the house so I couldn't hear any more of what he said.

87
00:05:16.435 --> 00:05:19.357
But I was so tired after the long journey, I didn't mind.

88
00:05:20.818 --> 00:05:22.900
John took me to the stable and unhitched me.

89
00:05:25.652 --> 00:05:30.143
Then he gave me a warm mash with lots of extra carrots, along with extra pats and
